; Rikishi research extension. Proposed vocabulary only; not part of upstream SUMO.
; No axiom here proves a mathematical free-energy or biological theorem.

(subclass RikishiVariationalInference Reasoning)
(documentation RikishiVariationalInference EnglishLanguage
  "A proposed class for finite-model posterior optimization processes in Rikishi. Its mathematical semantics and correspondence to Lean are obligations, not established axioms of SUMO.")

(subclass RikishiFiniteGenerativeModel Proposition)
(documentation RikishiFiniteGenerativeModel EnglishLanguage
  "A proposed representation of a finite prior and observation likelihood. Normalization and support conditions are checked by Rikishi numerical code, not implied by this class assertion.")

(instance RikishiBinaryInferenceExample RikishiVariationalInference)
(documentation RikishiBinaryInferenceExample EnglishLanguage
  "The example uses uniform binary prior, likelihoods 0.8 and 0.2, posterior 0.8 and 0.2, natural logarithms, and objective F(q)=sum q log(q/p(s,o)). This description supplies no proof transport from Lean.")
